  "description": "<p>This task is to change the 500 response that currently occurs in the following scenario to a '406 Not Acceptable'.</p>\n\n<p>To reproduce:</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create a versioned resource<br/>\ncurl -i -XPOST -H \"Slug: obj\" -H \"Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://mementoweb.org/ns#OriginalResource\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://mementoweb.org/ns#OriginalResource</a>&gt;; rel=\\\"type\\\"\" \"http://localhost:8080/rest/\"</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Request the resultant TimeMap with a bad \"Accept\" header<br/>\ncurl  <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/obj/fcr:versions\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/obj/fcr:versions</a> -H\"Accept: application/format-junk\"</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>&gt; Response: 500</p>\n\n<p>Note: Non-TimeMap resource respond with the correct 406.<br/>\nAlso, the above scenario responds correctly when using \"Accept: junk\".</p>",
